1. DISCRIMINATING CONTROLS -- does each pinned choice change the result?
==============================================================================
  [PASS] the naive SE is 35% smaller than Tukey-McLaughlin (0.6383 vs 0.9792) -- pinning the SE formula is not cosmetic
  [PASS] difference-then-trim and trim-then-difference differ by +0.2555 pts here -- naming 'trimmed mean' alone does not determine the estimate
  [PASS] ...and the PLAIN mean's gap is identically zero (-8.55e-15), so the non-additivity is a property of trimming, not of the data
  [PASS] sign-flipping `ned` changes the tail it reports (worst -23.50 -> -29.66, mean +1.70 -> -1.70) -- load-bearing, not decorative
  [PASS] assert_direction REJECTS contrast A with the arms swapped -- the orientation whose absence s3's amendment was filed to fix
  [PASS] ...and REJECTS a pair merge_ratio cannot order, rather than defaulting to the caller's argument order -- an unorderable pair is an unanswered question, not a direction of zero
  [PASS] CONTRAST A DOES NOT FLIP, and that is reported rather than assumed: the ratio moves 3.22 -> 3.18 under the swap (so the statistic is not reversal-invariant) but both clear p95 1.74, so run 14's gate failure is NOT an artifact of the orientation. The 10-of-28 flip is real and is measured in s5 on the cross-run family -- it is not a property of every pair, and asserting it here would have been asserting it where it happens not to hold
  [PASS] on the stored [0,1] field the harm rule counts 0 and in points it counts 5 -- this scorer converts first, so D14 s1d's unfalsifiable gate cannot recur here
  [PASS] the ratio gate FIRES on run 14 (3.22 > 1.74) and does NOT on run 13 (1.11 < 1.74) -- a gate firing on both or neither would be untested by this pair
  [PASS] run 14's contrast A is FLAT on location (CI [-1.90, +1.94] includes 0) yet FAILS a tail gate -- the exact case s3 was written to catch
  [PASS] the harmed-count bar is matched per row, not fixed: p95 is 7 on run 13 and 4 on run 14, because run 13's spread is wider -- so counts are NOT comparable across rows and must be quoted with their null

