==============================================================================
  [PASS] no config is evaluated twice within either run (28 and 28 rows, all distinct) -- so there is NO zero-treatment replicate on disk to calibrate the gate against, and decoding is bit-identical on re-run anyway (noise floor 0.000e+00), so one would be degenerate
  [PASS] all 28 cross-run pairs hold the config fixed and vary only the checkpoint, so s3's amendment orders them by run -- treatment is run 14
   checkpoint DiD (run 14 - run 13), the direction the design forces; normal-null p95 = 1.74
   config                          worst    wsd  ratio  merge
   keep=0.75 ink ORACLE           -80.85   6.63   5.43    NONE
   keep=0.75 random               -80.85   6.75   5.34    NONE
   keep=0.50 m=0.40 router        -74.47   7.18   4.62  m=0.40
   keep=1.00 m=0.20 router        -45.26   4.43   4.56  m=0.20
   keep=0.50 m=0.20 router        -50.00   6.53   3.41  m=0.20
   keep=0.80 router TWIN          -33.68   4.53   3.32    NONE

   rows with NO merging: 13/21 fire the gate   |   rows WITH merging: 6/7 fire
  [PASS] the gate fires on 13 of 21 contrasts that contain NO merging at all -- so clearing 1.74 is not evidence about merging
  [PASS] the single worst per-document loss in the whole sweep is -80.85 pts on `keep=0.75 ink ORACLE` -- keep=0.75, m=0, no merging -- and it has the highest ratio (5.43), above every merge row (max 4.62)
  [PASS] and it is not a small-denominator artifact: its winsorized sd is 6.63 pts, in line with the sweep, so the ratio is driven by a real 81 pt loss
  [PASS] the gate is not reversal-invariant: swapping which arm is 'treatment' flips the verdict on 10 of 28 configs (min(d) is one-sided) -- s3 pins direction per QUANTITY and leaves direction of the CONTRAST unwritten
  [PASS] the one comparator with neither pruning nor merging (`keep=1.00 router CONTROL`, keep=1.00 m=0) does pass at 1.47 -- so the gate is not firing on literally everything, and the failure is one of SPECIFICITY, not of sensitivity
   => the -72.34 page is real and both location estimators still hide it. But at
      the normal-null bar the gate cannot attribute it to merging, and run 17
      would fail this gate on rows where nothing is merged. The bar has to come
      from an active non-merge comparator, which is the `random` arm at the
      trained budget that run 17 already requires -- and that D14 measured as
      ABSENT from both runs. T3's fix and T4's missing arm are the same row.

